{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a1e157ccc2e788e2","name":"The Nyriaanan Clans","source":{"id":"source:reference-a1e157ccc2e788e2","title":"The Nyriaanan Clans","revision":21222,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:23:13Z","sha256":"c1b55e64dead6722c1df8abedc35959bbfe8244acdeb20d0a7d4a9b3080e80d0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21222","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Nyriaanan%20Clans&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a1e157ccc2e788e2","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Predators are not the only danger in the wilds of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"},". The native ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaanans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaanans"}," also patrol the wilderness. The original colonists are the crew of The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Starveil"]},", a Republic exploration vessel that crashes on the planet. Because of the ion storms in the planet's upper atmosphere, they are unable to leave the planet even after repairs are made to the ship. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Starveil"]}," crew's descendants go native and survive through a combination of ingenuity and determination. From a starting population of 52 individuals, their numbers grow over the millennia through childbirth and through the addition of other groups of survivors to their population.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Nyriaan's current ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaanan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaanan","referenceId":"reference:0f0737296e4d997d"}," population is unknown, but authorities estimate it to be anywhere between 1,200 and 2,000 individuals living in small communities. In truth, the figure is much larger. Although they have been confined to Nyriaan for generations, the planetary ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaanans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaanans"}," are biologically ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"},". Minor evolutionary changes are evident, such as their adaptation to the darkness prevalent on the planet's surface. Their spoken language is a mixture of High Galactic and Basic that has been combined into a unique colloquial dialect. Referred to as Nyriaanan by locals, the language is easily learned by anyone who speaks Basic and has a passing familiarity with High Galactic.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Nyriaanan Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Nonheroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaanan Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaanan_Scout","referenceId":"reference:6feb5ff1204dc512"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Heroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Finvarra"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Finvarra","referenceId":"reference:08f98393b536e96a"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of In